# Rule: Scroll animations & cockpit hooks

Shared scroll progress, cockpit integration, and home-v2 corridor-exit compositing. Changes affect Lenis, GSAP, HUD behavior, and the corridor→Services seam.

**Read first:** `sentinel/decisions/002-scroll-animation-architecture.md`, `sentinel/decisions/005-scroll-captured-content-reveal.md`, `sentinel/decisions/018-home-v2-depth-corridor.md`, `sentinel/decisions/021-corridor-exit-zoom-dissipate.md`.

**Process:** `sentinel/MAINTENANCE.md` - document contract changes with an ADR or decision addendum.

**Home-v2 corridor-exit invariant (ADR-021):** the production seam after the corridor epilogue is a **zoom-dissipate** — the docked R3F canvas plays a fly-into-sphere arc + particle scatter while the brandmark RIDES the sphere off-screen and then re-centres into the (now empty) Services section. `useCorridorExitScroll` owns the dissipate clock: raw progress is stretched over ~2 viewports (post 2026-06-16, ADR-021 follow-up; was 1.58), then eased into `--corridor-dissipate` / `dockProgress`. The hook ALSO writes a `data-services-brandmark` gate (`"hold"` then `"fade"`) + `--services-brandmark` (0..1) opacity var once the dock releases — `ProjectedBrandmarkActor` reads the gate to release the brandmark to CSS, which holds it fixed-centred in `#services` then fades it as `#continuum.top` crosses the `0.5 → 0.1 vh` band. The per-element reveal channels (`--services-header-in`, `--services-grid-in`, `--services-cta-in`) are GONE — `#services` was stripped of its header/cards/CTA in the same revision; restore those channels only if those elements come back. Keep the dock channel (`docked` / `dockProgress`) writes scoped to one hook; do not write `epilogueProgress` / `paintProgress` from the exit hook. The retired cover-plane sweep recipe (lower opaque plane covers a held canvas, first-read copy lives inside the cover) is preserved in `components/landing/home-v2/handoff-lab/` + `/test/handoff-a|b|c` and documented in ADR-021 — reuse that recipe verbatim if a later section needs an Active Theory / Hashgraph-class cover sweep; do not rebuild it.

**Seam pixel-field handoff (ADR-021 follow-up Phase 2, 2026-06-16):** on the capable path the SVG brandmark in `#services` is REPLACED by `CorridorSeamPixelField` — a fixed 2D canvas that paints the brandmark as a 3px gold/dawn pixel grid sampled from `BRANDMARK_FULL_PATHS` (same source the SVG glyph and `BrandmarkSilhouettePoints` use; ADR-014 single-source-of-truth). The dissolve begins the MOMENT the welded mark re-centres and shows itself — during the dock tail (`markCentred = docked ? dissipate >= MARK_CENTRED_DOCK_PROGRESS (0.85) : rawDissipate >= 0.999`), NOT only after the dock releases — and runs a long runway driven by `#continuum`'s approach (`seamMorph = smoothstep01((SEAM_MORPH_START_VH 1.9 - continuum.top/vh) / (1.9 - SEAM_MORPH_END_VH 0.1))`). The hook publishes `transform.seamMorph` + `--services-pixelate` + the scoping `data-services-pixelate="true"` attribute whenever `dockCapable && sectionNearDock && markCentred && continuum.top/vh < SEAM_MORPH_START_VH`; it may legitimately co-exist with `data-corridor-docked` (the morph opens before dock release by design). The pixel field reads `seamMorph` from the store; `home-v2.css` overrides the SVG glyph to `opacity: 0` and shows the canvas under `data-services-pixelate`. The actor-lifecycle gate (`data-services-brandmark` hold/fade + `--services-brandmark` opacity) is preserved unchanged for the SVG release + the fallback path. Square-pixel aesthetic is an INTENTIONAL borrow from `/test/gateway` (`ImageParticleGateway`) and an explicit ADR-015 exception — the seam field is OUTSIDE the brandmark painter cap (its own 2D canvas, its own rAF, its own brand-journey clock), so the cap (atmosphere + silhouette globals + substrate-sphere intelligence-layer mesh) is unchanged. All dispersal math lives in `lib/home-v2/seamPixelize.ts` and is unit-tested; do not duplicate the easing or the grid-snap inside the canvas component.

**Services ambient hold (ADR-021 addendum, 2026-06-19):** once the dock releases and the welded brandmark is centred in `#services`, an "inside-the-sphere" ambient haze keeps painting behind it for the hold runway. `useCorridorExitScroll` publishes `transform.servicesAmbient` + `transform.servicesAmbientLevel` (0..1 envelope, 1 across the hold, ramps to 0 with the continuum-approach fade), the `data-services-ambient="true"` `<html>` attribute, and a `--services-ambient` CSS var (mirrors `--services-brandmark` so haze + mark cross-fade). The body veil now reads a new `--corridor-exit-veil` (capped at `VEIL_AMBIENT_CAP = 0.45`) instead of the raw dissipate, so the fixed canvas stays visible underneath through both the dock tail and the hold; `data-corridor-exit` is held across both phases (`docked || servicesAmbient`). `home-v2.css` extends the fixed canvas promotion to `data-services-ambient`. R3F painters opt in via the engaged gate `active || armed || docked || servicesAmbient`: `MotionFollowerDriver` pins the smoothed dissipate at 1 during ambient so the camera/welded marks stay parked at the deepest inside-the-sphere pose; `FlyingCameraRig` treats `dockHeld = docked || servicesAmbient` as the dock-blend / reverse-snap signal; `ShellSubstrateGyro` composes `servicesAmbientOpacityMultiplier(servicesAmbientLevel)` onto the interior `mats.particle` cloud (surface materials still ride `dissipateOp` to 0) and suppresses the dock-time visibility/size boosts so the haze reads as distant background dust; `StaticStarfield` paints at the baseline opacity (no Build boost) scaled by `servicesAmbientLevel`; `BrandmarkPhysicsCoreActor` keeps the sim warm but forces `handoffFade = 0` so it never paints a duplicate mark behind the welded SVG / pixel field. The ambient hold timing constant `SERVICES_AMBIENT_HOLD_LEVEL = 0.48` lives in `lib/home-v2/epilogueTimeline.ts` with the multiplier helper and unit tests. Reverse-scroll safety: `useDepthScroll` mirrors the existing `DOCK_RELEASE_EPILOGUE_PROGRESS = 0.7` guard for the new flag — if the user scrolls back past the threshold while `prev.servicesAmbient` is still true, both the store flag and the `<html>` attribute / `--services-ambient` var are cleared in-line. Single-writer invariant intact: `useCorridorExitScroll` SETS the ambient channel; `useDepthScroll` only CLEARS it. Fallback path (`!dockCapable`) never engages the flag.

**Hero → Thoughtform seam invariant (ADR-022 v8):** the hero → corridor seam is a **ToyFight curtain reveal** — the **hero is the moving layer** (`.hero`, `position: relative; z-index: 4`) that scrolls up and off the first viewport, uncovering the corridor's parked `ThoughtformCompassGate` frame held **frozen** behind it (`.home-corridor-host` z:3). NOT the inverse (v7's mistake: a held hero with the corridor rising to cover it), and NEVER a proxy/copy of the second section (v6's mistake). The freeze: `useLandingScroll` toggles `html[data-corridor-entry]` while the corridor stage top is below the viewport top, and `home-v2.css` makes `.home-v2-stage__sticky` `position: fixed; inset: 0` under that flag. At the handoff the flag clears and native sticky resumes at the same `top: 0`, with no transform on the sticky cell and never on `.home-v2-stage`. The hero may receive only a tiny capped inertial `translateY` correction for ToyFight-like smoothness; document scroll, corridor `progress` / `paintProgress` / `epilogueProgress` / `dockProgress`, and the hero video opacity remain untouched. Hero video stays opaque, never scaled/faded (ADR-008 Rule 3, gateway shield). ADR-022 history documents every superseded approach (v6 proxy sweep, v7 held-hero parallax/counter-translate) and its artifact.
